& \therefore \frac{\mathrm{~T}_2}{\mathrm{~T}_1}=\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{M}_1}{\mathrm{M}_2}}=\sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{I}_1}{\mathrm{I}_2}}=\sqrt{\frac{2.5}{10}}=\frac{1}{2} \\
& \therefore \mathrm{~T}_2=\frac{\mathrm{T}_1}{2}=\frac{\mathrm{T}}{2}
\end{aligned}$

